00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:07.840
Can we- can we cut to commercial break

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.800
Cut- cut to commercial

00:03:08.800 --> 00:03:10.260
CUT TO COMMERCIAL FUCKING BREAK!

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:11.380
*BEEP

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:14.300
(80's commercial music starts playing)

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:18.520
Lawry's seasoned SALT

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.160
NOT GOING BACK OUT THERE

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:21.600
ARE YOU SEEING THIS!?

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:25.220
I DIDN'T KNOW PEOPLE WHO WATCH ANIME WERE A BUNCH OF BRAIN DEAD MONKEYS WITHOUT EYES!

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:27.580
AND WHOSE GREAT IDEA WAS IT TO LET FUJOSHIS VOTE!?

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.680
Stand aside solar and wind

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:32.600
could SALT be the amazing energy source of the future

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:34.980
Salt, tears of the earth

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:36.020
*BEEP

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.540
Alright I'm back guys, I'm back

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.940
We don't have much long today but before i leave you all do you want to hear a joke?

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:43.560
Your taste in anime.

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:47.600
*Laughing and applause*
Thank you very much I will see you all next year!

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:48.660
*LONGER BEEP

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.100
Alright Crunchyroll let's have a little serious talk about these awards.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:53.960
I can see what you were going for

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.400
And these awards did seem like a fun little idea if done correctly (agreed)

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.560
But there was always going to be a problem hosting an award show

00:04:00.560 --> 00:04:04.400
designed to showcase the best of anime coming out of the previous year.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.800
Decided entirely by popular vote

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:10.120
And boy did that problem rear its head in these results

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:12.300
Even the nomination system you had before

00:04:12.300 --> 00:04:14.720
With your judges submitting blind nominations

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:19.380
Was always going to skew nominations towards popularity before voting had even begun

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:22.000
And as much as there were some unexpected nominations

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:24.560
And well... weird nominations

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.080
The vast pool of anime last year were definitely not represented

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:33.120
Personally I do not think a popular vote should be the entire basis of an award ceremony like this

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.640
I think alot of us who have watched more anime than Yuri on ice last year

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:41.360
Can safely say that most these winners are not the best thing to come out of their categories

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.560
but instead are just the most popular shows in their respective categories.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.340
There is alot of potential here

00:04:46.340 --> 00:04:48.520
And i hope there is a better system next year.

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:50.560
And hey my door are always open, just saying.

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.160
But enough of the negative

00:04:52.160 --> 00:04:54.440
To offset all the salt that's being thrown around

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:56.360
I taught i'd host my own anime awards

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.640
That i hope everyone will be able to agree with

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:01.800
*music play*

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.720
